    <div class="lux-reader-rule"></div>
    <section class="lux-reader-hero"><div class="lux-reader-hero-copy"><div class="lux-reader-meta-grid"><span>Caviar Academy</span><span>CAVIAR ACADEMY · 2026</span></div><h1 id="lux-reader-title">How to Keep Your Caviar at Its Best After Opening</h1><p class="lux-reader-summary">Opened your caviar but can’t finish it? Here’s how to keep it at its best.</p></div><figure class="lux-reader-cover"><img width="933" height="1400" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" src="<?php echo esc_url(get_template_directory_uri() . '/assets/media/academy/caviar-after-opening-cover.webp'); ?>" alt="How to Keep Your Caviar at Its Best After Opening"></figure></section>
    <section class="lux-reader-content"><aside class="lux-reader-aside"><a href="<?php echo esc_url(luxureat_static_url('en/blog', '')); ?>">Back to Knowledge Blog</a></aside><div class="lux-reader-copy"><section class="lux-reader-section lux-reader-section-opening"><p>Caviar is exceptionally delicate. Once opened, exposure to air and changes in temperature can quickly affect its flavour, texture and freshness.</p><p>A few simple rules will help preserve its quality:</p></section><section class="lux-reader-section" id="article-section-0"><h2>Keep it very cold</h2><p>Store caviar in the coldest part of your refrigerator, ideally between -2°C and +2°C. Never freeze it.</p><div class="lux-reader-section-media"><figure><img width="933" height="1400" loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="<?php echo esc_url(get_template_directory_uri() . '/assets/media/academy/caviar-after-opening-cold.webp'); ?>" alt="How to Keep Your Caviar at Its Best After Opening"></figure></div></section><section class="lux-reader-section" id="article-section-1"><h2>Use the right spoon</h2><p>Choose a mother-of-pearl, horn, glass or suitable non-metallic spoon to enjoy the caviar without interfering with its delicate flavour.</p><div class="lux-reader-section-media"><figure><img width="933" height="1400" loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="<?php echo esc_url(get_template_directory_uri() . '/assets/media/academy/caviar-after-opening-spoon.webp'); ?>" alt="How to Keep Your Caviar at Its Best After Opening"></figure></div></section><section class="lux-reader-section" id="article-section-2"><h2>Limit contact with air</h2><p>After serving, gently place a piece of food-safe cling film directly over the surface of the remaining caviar, removing as much trapped air as possible. Then close the tin securely and return it immediately to the refrigerator.</p><div class="lux-reader-section-media"><figure><img width="933" height="1400" loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="<?php echo esc_url(get_template_directory_uri() . '/assets/media/academy/caviar-after-opening-care.webp'); ?>" alt="How to Keep Your Caviar at Its Best After Opening"></figure></div></section><section class="lux-reader-section" id="article-section-3"><h2>Enjoy it quickly</h2><p>Once opened, caviar is best consumed as soon as possible and generally within 2–3 days, provided it has been continuously and correctly refrigerated.</p></section><section class="lux-reader-section" id="article-section-4"><h2>The golden rule</h2><p>Cold temperature, minimal air exposure and careful handling.</p><p>Because great caviar deserves to taste exactly as it should — until the very last spoonful.</p></section></div></section>
